    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0871" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">093.612/57: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-17">April 17,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received April 17—11:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1317. Moscow papers for April 15 announce the awarding of the Order of Suvorov
                    Second Class to General Connolly and of various other Soviet orders to 33
                    American officers and men of the Persian Gulf Command “for the successful
                    fulfillment of the instructions of the American Command in the Persian Gulf in
                    transporting munitions supplies and foodstuffs to the Soviet Union which have
                    provided great assistance to the Red Army in the struggle with the German
                    Fascist invaders.”<anchor n="41" xml:id="d788-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d788-f1" n="41" xml:id="d788-f1-content">
                <p>In a letter of April 16 from People’s Commissar of Foreign Trade Mikoyan to
                    Ambassador Harriman, the final paragraph stated that these decorations “express
                    the friendship, which is growing stronger, of our great countries in the
                    struggle against the common enemy for the better future of freedom-loving
                    people.” (093.612/76)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
